  {
   "n": 15,
   "type": "NAT",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0",
   "html": "<p>Consider a threshold detector with input <em>R</em> = <em>X</em> + <em>N</em>, where <em>X</em> is the signal level at the input of the detector due to transmitted binary data and <em>N</em> is a noise variable which is characterised by the probability density function f<sub>N</sub>(n) = 0.5e<sup>–</sup>|<sup>n</sup>|.<br />\n<em>X</em> takes the values : +1 with probability of 1/3<br />\n–1 with probability of 2/3<br />\nIf the threshold value of the detector is decided in an optimum way using maximum a posteriori<br />\n(MAP) criteria, the value of optimum threshold voltage is _________. [Rounded off to two decimal places]</p>",
